 10.6, "analyst_adjustment": -0.6, "key_factors": ["Haaland's dominant fundraising edge ($11.1M raised vs. $474K for Hull)", "Expert ratings uniformly favor Democrats, mostly Solid or Safe D", "Polls show a consistent Haaland lead, though with some spread (6 to 17 points)", "Prediction markets price Haaland at roughly 90-95% to win"], "rationale": "Every available signal points the same direction: Haaland leads by high single digits in polling averages, has an overwhelming money advantage, and all six expert ratings put the race in the Democratic column, with markets pricing her win probability above 90 percent. The open seat removes incumbency protection, but New Mexico's Democratic lean and the fundamentals still favor Haaland comfortably.", "watch": "A competitive debate performance by Hull or a shift in the race toward affordability issues like data centers and utilities could tighten the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's open governor's race features Democrat Deb Haaland against Republican Gregg Hull to succeed term-limited Governor Michelle Lujan Grisham. Haaland holds a large financial advantage, raising more than $11 million compared with under half a million for Hull, and recent polls show her leading by margins ranging from 6 to 17 points. Expert raters across the board place the race in the Democratic column, with most calling it Solid or Safe Democratic. Prediction markets similarly price Haaland as a heavy favorite. The race has centered on debates, which remain unscheduled, and on issues including data centers, healthcare, housing, and utility affordability. Hull has hovered around the mid-40s or lower in polling, and the state's Democratic lean continues to shape the contest. The main uncertainty is whether Hull can use the debate stage and affordability concerns to narrow the gap in the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.958, "margin": 10.0}]}